From: Upstream <netdev@vger.kernel.org>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: fix foe_check_time allocation size

ppe->foe_check_time is a u16 array indexed by the FOE hash up to
ppe_num_entries, but it was allocated with devm_kzalloc(eth->dev,
ppe_num_entries, ...) -- i.e. only ppe_num_entries bytes instead of
ppe_num_entries * sizeof(*foe_check_time). The buffer is under-allocated
by half, so writes via ppe->foe_check_time[hash] = now in the flow
offload hot path overrun the allocation and corrupt adjacent heap
memory once flows populate the upper half of the table.

Multiply by sizeof(*foe_check_time), matching the sibling foe_flow
allocation.

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
index 5c9dff6bcc..8fb8ecf909 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
@@ -1578,7 +1578,8 @@ int airoha_ppe_init(struct airoha_eth *eth)
 			return -ENOMEM;
 	}

-	ppe->foe_check_time = devm_kzalloc(eth->dev, ppe_num_entries,
+	ppe->foe_check_time = devm_kzalloc(eth->dev,
+					   ppe_num_entries * sizeof(*ppe->foe_check_time),
 					   GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!ppe->foe_check_time)
 		return -ENOMEM;
